#!/bin/sh
# micke-help — the in-guest manual page: the desktop loop, one line per helper.
#
# WHY: the session_shell tool description is the agent's only manual, but an
# agent that orients from `agent-desktop --help` / `agent-desktop skills` in
# the guest sees a competing loop that mentions none of the micke helpers —
# and the skills are compiled into the agent-desktop binary (location:
# "embedded"), so they cannot carry a micke skill. This script is the manual
# agents can find FROM inside the session: the same recipe the tool
# description leads with, plus one line per helper.
#
# stdout: the manual. Exit 0 always; writes nothing to stderr, no files.
# Takes no arguments (extra ones are ignored — an agent typing
# `micke-help type` still wants the whole page).

cat <<'EOF'
micke — the desktop loop (same recipe the session_shell manual leads with)

  micke-chromium <url>
    -> micke-find <text> [--role R]        REF<TAB>ROLE<TAB>NAME per match
    -> agent-desktop click "<ref>"         ref = first column of micke-find
    -> micke-type '<text>'                 click the field FIRST, then this
    -> micke-key <combo>                   e.g. ctrl+r
    -> micke-state                         verify; repeat

Helpers:
  micke-chromium <url>              launch chromium (required flags pre-baked)
  micke-find <text> [--role R]      find a click target: ONE filtered snapshot
  micke-type '<text>'               type into the focused field: clipboard + ctrl+v
  micke-key <combo>                 ONE key combo (agent-desktop press SIGSEGVs chromium here)
  micke-state                       {"alive":..,"title":..,"url":..,"refs":..}; exit 1 = no browser
  micke-page-text <url> [--links]   page CONTENT as small JSON (not the a11y tree)

Rules:
  - Verify with micke-state (title/url/refs), never screenshots; a dead
    browser is otherwise silent (list-windows [], session_list still ready).
  - Headless `agent-desktop type` is refused on real pages (POLICY_DENIED /
    ACTION_NOT_SUPPORTED); `agent-desktop --headed type` also works and is
    the agent-desktop-native alternative to micke-type.
  - Below-fold targets: `click`/`scroll-to` on them can time out in preparatory
    scroll (TIMEOUT/not_delivered) — keyboard-scroll first (`micke-key ctrl+Home/ctrl+End/PageDown`), re-find (refs are snapshot-scoped), then click.
  - `agent-desktop` exits non-zero when its JSON envelope says ok:false —
    `set -e` and `&&` are trustworthy.
  - Every session_shell call is a fresh bash: cwd and env do NOT persist.
    Make each command self-contained (`cd /x && cmd`).
EOF
